The encoder derives from answerdotai/ModernBERT-base by Answer.AI, LightOn and collaborators.
Base model: https://huggingface.co/answerdotai/ModernBERT-base (Apache-2.0).
Paper: Warner et al., Smarter, Better, Faster, Longer: A Modern Bidirectional Encoder for Fast,
Memory Efficient, and Long Context Finetuning and Inference. https://arxiv.org/abs/2412.13663

Training data sources retain their own licenses:
BANKING77 — PolyAI, Casanueva et al. (2020), CC-BY-4.0.
https://github.com/PolyAI-LDN/task-specific-datasets
MASSIVE — Amazon Science, CC-BY-4.0.
https://huggingface.co/datasets/AmazonScience/massive
Typed Decisions — LocalLLaMA/codelion, Apache-2.0.
https://huggingface.co/datasets/LocalLLaMA/typed-decisions

Transformations include grouped splits, candidate descriptions, candidate sampling,
option shuffling, abstention augmentation, and normalization of rounded soft targets.
Original third-party datasets are not bundled in the model release. Revisions and
transformation hashes are recorded in data/manifests.
DecisionBench is evaluation-only; its metadata declares license "other". No benchmark
records are redistributed, relicensed or incorporated into training.
